                    {
                        "recommendationid": "41409068",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198066590240",
                            "num_reviews": 3404,
                            "playtime_forever": 37,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 37,
                            "last_played": 1523411031
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\n[i] Only issue I experienced on the Oculus Rift is that you have to press trigger and push down on the joystick to select menu items. You only need standing room, not full roomscale. [/i]\n\nI don't think this is a great VR puzzle game, but it's not bad for being free. The graphics are subpar. The color scheme will kind of hurt your eyes at first, but I got used to it. The control scheme is also less than desirable. You press trigger to grab & the joystick down to whatever direction to change colors and then your other hand you press trigger to teleport. Grab button switches hands for a very odd and frustrating reason. There's also an option to dash, but I wouldn't advise it as you have to be precise with your movements at times to avoid the lasers. The sounds are also not very good. If all the above issues had been polished, this might have been a very good puzzle game.\n\nI believe there are 12 levels to clear. It's a laser color puzzle game that we've all seen before. However, there are a few twists. The main one being is that you can control what color gets sent out and you have to avoid the lasers or figure ways around them. There's also leaderboards to brag about how you played it more than once and you were able to do it faster the second time around.\n\nRate 6/10. It's free and you can even download the demo if you just can't commit to downloading the whole game for free :)",
